OP: You need to decide what you're going to use for your main non-spell 
weapon though Gehennom-- Magicbane or Fire Brand-- and enchant that 
weapon. Personally, for the time being I'd carry MB and switch to FB 
for melee with anything other than Ls or yellow nagas, and I'd enchant 
FB to +7 right now (and I'd advance the weapon skill all the way now as 
well). Before you go for Rodney you can decide how you'll manage the 
Amulet run and make the appropriate preparations. I'd recommend 
switching to MB once you have the amulet; whether it should be +7 for 
the damage ot +0 - +2 for the stunning is your choice. I've ascended 
several Wizards wielding unenchanted MB all through hell and the 
planes, so it's certainly possible without stellar Nethack skills.

You also need to do something about your armor class; aim for around -
20 before you pay off the priest in the Valley, which will require 
maybe 5-8 or so blessed scrolls of enchant armor. nb, don't enchant 
those gauntlets, because their small penalty for spellcasting (even at 
your level, even with your helm of brilliance) isn't acceptable once 
you have the Amulet and your mana effectively becomes limited. Plan on 
switching to plain gloves or GoD and enchanting those instead.


